 productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Global Net Lease, Inc. is a small-cap real estate business with a $1.5B market cap on $495M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +9% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +105.1pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $189M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 38 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -11.3% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 20.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 9.4% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 1243% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"